WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:58.550 --> 02:01.310
We'll stand out too much if you stay in those.

02:08.360 --> 02:11.350
Let's hurry before those people come back.

02:16.260 --> 02:21.200
Our Fox Deity, Pursues

02:25.640 --> 02:27.230
Let's go out there for now.

02:27.540 --> 02:29.700
It's better if we stay in crowded places.

02:40.420 --> 02:41.450
Shiro-chan?

02:44.190 --> 02:46.960
It's all right. I'll do something about it.

02:56.470 --> 02:57.030
Toru.

03:00.910 --> 03:02.930
It's you, Aki.

03:03.340 --> 03:04.610
What are you doing here?

03:04.680 --> 03:07.080
I should be asking you that.

03:07.750 --> 03:10.690
Well, whatever. I'm on my
way home from cram school.

03:10.690 --> 03:11.380
Oh.

03:11.490 --> 03:14.940
What did you do to make
those monks come after you?

03:16.820 --> 03:20.590
They're actually a bunch of evil cultists.

03:20.830 --> 03:21.760
That's why...

03:22.530 --> 03:24.290
Evil cultists?

03:25.300 --> 03:27.790
So where is she from?

03:28.970 --> 03:32.840
Uh, Sri Jayawardenapura Kotte?

03:33.170 --> 03:34.940
In other words, you don't want to say.

03:39.510 --> 03:41.140
You have your reasons, right?

03:42.580 --> 03:43.610
You don't?

03:44.690 --> 03:45.350
I do.

03:47.420 --> 03:52.990
So for now, you want to help
her escape those evil cultists?

03:53.230 --> 03:54.060
Yup.

03:55.130 --> 03:56.260
Oh...

03:58.130 --> 04:02.470
Fine, I'll help you with your little elopement.

04:02.700 --> 04:04.370
You can leave it to me.

04:10.080 --> 04:10.770
Naguma-san!

04:13.210 --> 04:14.010
There he is!

04:14.420 --> 04:17.540
If we capture him, we can lure the Byakki out!

04:38.140 --> 04:39.470
Takagami Toru-san.

04:39.810 --> 04:41.540
We need you to come with us.

04:46.810 --> 04:48.980
Who are you guys?

04:59.990 --> 05:02.990
What are you going to do?
They're leaving on a bus.

05:03.200 --> 05:05.290
Don't worry.

05:05.900 --> 05:07.230
Look, it's here.

05:12.740 --> 05:13.830
Get in.

05:18.850 --> 05:24.650
I've always wanted a customer to
tell me to "follow that car up ahead!"

05:25.120 --> 05:27.380
Are you guys detectives?

05:27.560 --> 05:30.050
Unfortunately, I'm just a
member of the Overseers.

05:31.890 --> 05:33.450
Are you a god?

05:33.900 --> 05:35.020
I am.

05:35.300 --> 05:36.630
What about that woman?

05:36.900 --> 05:37.730
She's Bekira.

05:38.400 --> 05:40.160
She's not a god, but...

05:40.370 --> 05:42.340
I quit being a human.

05:44.410 --> 05:46.970
Who are the "Overseers?"

05:47.210 --> 05:52.050
Well, things exist that are dangerous in
the hands of ignorant people or yokai.

05:52.050 --> 05:57.610
We collect items endangering the
world of man and watch over them.

05:57.890 --> 06:00.510
We sometimes seal or destroy them as well.

06:00.860 --> 06:01.820
I see.

06:02.320 --> 06:04.590
We sometimes entrust it to particular individuals.

06:04.730 --> 06:06.660
Like with the Sakasaen and Mubyo.

06:08.300 --> 06:10.490
Mubyo doesn't have it anymore.

06:11.200 --> 06:17.400
So the Overseers want to take Shiro,
I mean the Byakki, to watch over?

06:17.670 --> 06:19.700
She's dangerous if left to herself.

06:20.480 --> 06:25.940
As if inversely proportional to her high
offensive capabilities, her defense is weak.

06:26.350 --> 06:29.750
She's a very unstable being and
the slightest tap can kill her.

06:30.020 --> 06:31.920
How do you know that?

06:32.290 --> 06:35.020
The Byakki had died once in the past.

06:35.620 --> 06:37.130
In the land of the gods.

06:37.130 --> 06:38.590
The land of the gods?

06:38.960 --> 06:40.930
But I revived her.

06:41.660 --> 06:46.690
Granted, reviving the dead is one of
the most serious taboos we have.

06:47.370 --> 06:48.840
Why did you do it then?

06:49.640 --> 06:54.340
When the Byakki dies, energy fields collapse,
forcing open the "Boundaries" of the area.

06:54.740 --> 06:58.410
It throws the land into confusion
almost indefinitely as a result.

06:58.680 --> 07:01.550
Is that why you committed the taboo?

07:01.950 --> 07:08.180
Of course, it caused me to be afflicted
with an illness for the rest of eternity.

07:08.390 --> 07:13.190
That's why I'm always with
him as his personal doctor.

07:13.260 --> 07:14.130
Personal doctor?

07:14.230 --> 07:16.360
Yes, she's a witch doctor.

07:17.170 --> 07:21.900
Her job is to treat astral symptoms using sorcery.

07:22.740 --> 07:25.000
She's also the one who drew
those tattoos on the Byakki.

07:26.440 --> 07:31.040
But that is why we have
watched the Byakki ever since.

07:31.810 --> 07:34.350
But she was stolen from us the other day.

07:34.350 --> 07:35.370
Stolen?

07:35.820 --> 07:36.370
By whom?

07:36.680 --> 07:37.650
We don't know.

07:38.290 --> 07:40.720
That's why we're letting the
Byakki run free for now.

07:41.020 --> 07:45.220
The tattoos emit a very special signal.

07:45.530 --> 07:49.860
As long as we can follow it,
we'll know where she is.

07:50.060 --> 07:56.490
But the signal gets blocked when
she's wrapped with enchanted cloth.

07:57.940 --> 08:00.910
The original purpose of the tattoos is...

08:01.010 --> 08:05.600
...to prevent the Byakki from having
a completely empty stomach.

08:05.810 --> 08:08.440
Do you know what the Byakki mainly eats?

08:08.950 --> 08:12.150
The life energies of other organisms.

08:12.850 --> 08:18.950
Unable to create her own life force,
the Byakki constantly hungers for it.

08:19.830 --> 08:22.590
If we leave her to herself,
she'll attack anyone who comes close to her.

08:23.230 --> 08:28.430
Her intelligence is low,
so she can't tell right from wrong.

08:28.970 --> 08:32.630
That is exactly why she needs a
"command center" in the form of a "parent."

08:32.940 --> 08:33.700
A parent?

08:33.940 --> 08:35.570
It's Toru!

08:35.880 --> 08:36.840
Toru?

08:38.080 --> 08:40.740
So that's why she listens to Toru.

08:40.920 --> 08:46.850
Yes. The Byakki assigns the one
she first sees as her parent.

08:46.950 --> 08:49.460
Imprinting...

08:49.460 --> 08:50.150
Yes.

08:50.560 --> 08:52.990
That's why she is the proof of the lord of the oni.

08:53.590 --> 08:56.060
The one who becomes the parent is
worthy of becoming the lord of the oni.

08:56.730 --> 08:59.390
That's why Princess Enju wants the Byakki.

08:59.830 --> 09:04.500
But through some conspiracy,
Toru-kun became the parent instead.

09:05.340 --> 09:09.140
That's why she'll continue to
follow Toru-kun no matter what.

09:10.750 --> 09:11.580
Really?

09:11.580 --> 09:14.100
Yeah! He then said...

09:25.530 --> 09:26.320
Stop!

09:29.130 --> 09:29.730
Hurry!

09:29.730 --> 09:30.630
W-Wait!

09:31.900 --> 09:34.390
Are you sure you don't want to check the specs?

09:34.870 --> 09:37.430
I can't sacrifice innocent people for no reason.

09:39.510 --> 09:42.840
You almost sound like a real sister.

09:44.610 --> 09:46.670
Just tell me what I must be careful of.

09:47.920 --> 09:49.010
This product...

09:49.320 --> 09:53.520
The Dema is a simplified shikigami that
acts only with its ingrained aggression.

09:53.850 --> 09:55.010
It has no soul.

09:55.620 --> 10:01.820
A very powerful being specially made it
to follow your orders.

10:02.860 --> 10:06.230
But I'll keep the price low.
You're a regular after all.

10:06.630 --> 10:08.930
Why are you doing so much for us?

10:09.500 --> 10:11.660
The blood of the oni flows in my veins.

10:12.140 --> 10:16.800
I want to see you restore the oni
clan and also humiliate the gods...

10:16.940 --> 10:21.240
If you can manage to do all of that,
it'll make me feel good. That's all.

10:21.920 --> 10:23.210
Who is the culprit?

10:23.580 --> 10:25.980
Who sent Shiro to Toru?!

10:26.390 --> 10:27.350
I don't know.

10:27.890 --> 10:32.420
Someone who will benefit from having
a human become the Byakki's "parent."

10:32.930 --> 10:34.900
Why would anyone do that?!

10:35.700 --> 10:39.220
It could be to prevent the
birth of the lord of the oni.

10:39.670 --> 10:42.000
It could also be a personal
grudge against Toru-kun.

10:42.800 --> 10:45.270
But those are just guesses.

10:45.670 --> 10:46.770
They will pay for this...

10:47.680 --> 10:50.110
Can you wash the rice?

10:59.690 --> 11:00.920
Wow...

11:01.290 --> 11:05.050
She's actually using water and her
hands instead of detergent and a brush.

11:07.900 --> 11:08.790
I'm finished.

11:09.230 --> 11:10.700
What should I do next?

11:10.830 --> 11:13.600
Can you cut the carrot into fine slices?

11:14.170 --> 11:15.100
Understood.

11:20.710 --> 11:24.470
When she first came here, she
couldn't tell lettuce from cabbage.

11:24.650 --> 11:29.450
She busted holes in pots, broke
dishes every time she washed them...

11:29.850 --> 11:31.580
And look at her now!

11:32.490 --> 11:33.710
Good job, Ko!

11:34.390 --> 11:35.580
You've come a long way!

11:39.360 --> 11:41.560
Hey, uh...

11:42.230 --> 11:43.530
What are you doing?

11:43.730 --> 11:45.530
I am turning the carrot into fine slices.

11:45.800 --> 11:47.560
I know I said that, but...

11:54.380 --> 11:55.240
Hello?

11:55.980 --> 11:57.970
Oh, you're from Toru's school.

11:58.580 --> 12:02.740
It's just that Toru-kun's backpack was left here.

12:03.450 --> 12:09.190
Yes, I tried looking for him, but all of
the students have already gone home.

12:10.060 --> 12:13.960
I hope he's not involved
with some kind of accident.

12:16.500 --> 12:18.430
Accident...

12:21.200 --> 12:23.690
She was just asking if Toru was back yet.

12:24.310 --> 12:25.770
By the way, where's Ku?

12:26.040 --> 12:27.560
Out on a walk as usual.

12:27.780 --> 12:28.800
As usual...

12:29.080 --> 12:31.010
It's taking a bit too long for a walk,
don't you think?

12:31.080 --> 12:32.770
I guess so...

12:34.720 --> 12:36.110
Did something happen?

12:47.900 --> 12:50.760
I see. So Toru didn't go there.

12:51.070 --> 12:52.030
All right.

12:57.840 --> 13:02.370
I'm going to some places where Toru might be.

13:02.880 --> 13:05.070
I really doubt he'd get caught in an accident...

13:06.810 --> 13:08.980
I can be such a worrywart.

13:08.980 --> 13:10.140
I want to go, too.

13:14.660 --> 13:16.780
This is all I have left.

13:17.390 --> 13:19.150
We'll have to walk the rest of the way.

13:21.230 --> 13:23.960
Let's go to Ogami-san's place
and ask if we can stay over.

13:36.080 --> 13:37.570
I feel much better now.

13:41.080 --> 13:42.680
Let me go!

13:42.680 --> 13:43.650
Contact the others.

13:44.150 --> 13:45.310
We just captured Toru-kun.

13:45.550 --> 13:46.140
Right away.

13:46.690 --> 13:48.020
I said, let go!

13:48.260 --> 13:49.380
Let me go!

13:49.560 --> 13:51.650
What are you doing to a little kid?

13:57.360 --> 13:59.300
Hi, Toru-chan! What's up!

13:59.470 --> 14:00.660
How're you doing?

14:01.700 --> 14:03.500
Okay, I guess.

14:03.970 --> 14:05.770
Where are you going at this hour?

14:06.140 --> 14:08.870
I wanted to go to Noboru's school.

14:10.710 --> 14:12.510
Anyway, want this?

14:12.510 --> 14:13.310
Mubyo-chan!

14:22.690 --> 14:26.350
Oh, geez. Attacking from behind is cheating.

14:26.490 --> 14:28.620
Don't you think so?

14:29.260 --> 14:30.090
Yeah...

14:32.670 --> 14:35.690
I thought I told you to stay put, Shiro-chan!

14:37.040 --> 14:38.560
You're that person from yesterday...

14:51.550 --> 14:52.420
What is that?!

14:54.660 --> 14:56.180
What are you, stupid?

14:56.590 --> 14:59.080
How could you summon Kagutsuchi here?

14:59.630 --> 15:01.060
It'll be dangerous here.

15:01.460 --> 15:02.830
You need to leave this place, Toru-chan.

15:03.560 --> 15:04.050
But!

15:04.500 --> 15:05.520
Just go!

15:08.700 --> 15:10.690
Thanks, Mubyo-chan!

15:13.810 --> 15:15.300
Now then...

15:19.950 --> 15:23.380
Let's keep things simple and start off with water.

15:42.470 --> 15:44.660
That's so effective.

15:46.310 --> 15:48.710
It's been a while, substitute of Mubyo.

15:51.450 --> 15:53.350
You're one of the Overseers!

15:53.350 --> 15:54.540
What are you doing here?

15:54.750 --> 15:56.050
It's not just me.

15:57.180 --> 15:58.050
The tenko!

15:58.390 --> 16:00.680
What are you doing here?

16:00.890 --> 16:02.120
But this is perfect timing.

16:02.290 --> 16:05.620
May I borrow your Sakasaen?

16:12.900 --> 16:14.420
Wait right there.

16:18.840 --> 16:21.000
I wonder where Ogami-san is.

16:21.140 --> 16:22.200
Hey...

16:25.810 --> 16:29.980
Aren't you Toru? Yeah, Takagami's little brother.

16:31.020 --> 16:34.390
No, never! I'm never lending it out!

16:34.820 --> 16:38.780
It'll be possible to capture the
Byakki if we have the Sakasaen.

16:39.260 --> 16:43.290
If she tries to absorb life energies,
it'll just go in reverse instead.

16:43.460 --> 16:46.960
I can't do that! Just because
you're with the Overseers...

16:47.030 --> 16:47.830
Because...

16:50.070 --> 16:52.370
Wait, why are you with him anyway?

16:52.940 --> 16:56.240
Knowing your personality, I'm
surprised you can be around him.

16:56.580 --> 16:57.840
What's that supposed to mean?

16:59.050 --> 17:02.020
The Kugen fox doesn't remember me.

17:03.020 --> 17:06.110
What?! You don't remember?!

17:08.060 --> 17:12.120
I don't believe you. Did you go senile after
being sealed for a couple of centuries?

17:12.460 --> 17:14.290
He's an Overseer!

17:14.600 --> 17:18.550
They've confiscated and sealed stuff
for as long as anyone can remember.

17:18.930 --> 17:19.760
That's why...

17:42.560 --> 17:45.180
Are you Tsukuyomi?

17:45.590 --> 17:47.530
You finally remembered.

17:47.900 --> 17:49.950
Kugen fox of the Mizuchi.

17:50.360 --> 17:55.830
Seeing how you forgot who sealed you,
it looks like you've gone soft in the head.

17:56.270 --> 17:58.670
How could you expect me to know?

17:58.840 --> 18:01.170
I don't remember you being that small.

18:01.410 --> 18:05.170
You think I'll look the same
after a few centuries?

18:07.610 --> 18:10.280
Calm down, both of you.

18:10.750 --> 18:14.780
Who do you think will get in the most
trouble if you start fighting? Me!

18:14.890 --> 18:16.580
Why would I fight?

18:16.920 --> 18:21.090
Because it's your chance to get revenge
for a grudge from centuries back?

18:21.700 --> 18:23.250
I don't have any grudges.

18:24.970 --> 18:29.030
So it seems you became more
than just soft in the head...

18:29.340 --> 18:33.740
Never mind that. You just reminded me
of something else.

18:34.580 --> 18:37.670
I now know why the Byakki is white.

18:38.310 --> 18:38.900
Oh?

18:39.450 --> 18:43.820
White is the color of clouds,
the things that hide the sun.

18:44.120 --> 18:48.790
Since you gods exalt the sun goddess as the
highest among yourselves, it signifies rebellion.

18:48.790 --> 18:50.650
It's the color of the "defiant ones."

18:51.260 --> 18:57.820
That means the Byakki is the
symbol of all who defy the gods.

18:58.630 --> 19:01.900
And you hate that.

19:02.240 --> 19:02.930
So?

19:03.400 --> 19:05.840
You said the Byakki died once.

19:06.270 --> 19:10.140
Why was the Byakki in the land
of the gods in the first place?

19:10.540 --> 19:14.000
You brought her to your lands and killed her.

19:16.380 --> 19:18.720
I knew something was out of place.

19:19.320 --> 19:23.450
And you said you revived her because
it messed with the energy fields?

19:23.620 --> 19:27.060
You make it sound like you're doing
everyone a favor. Don't make me laugh.

19:27.560 --> 19:32.360
It only happened because you were all ignorant,
reckless, and lacked any speck of foresight.

19:32.900 --> 19:35.400
You said you were afflicted with an illness...

19:35.400 --> 19:39.300
All that happened was your powers
depleted and you shrunk in size!

19:41.280 --> 19:42.900
You got what you deserved.

19:43.510 --> 19:45.140
It's the curse of the Byakki!

19:45.750 --> 19:50.840
Kugen, for a fox, you're short-tempered,
stubborn and simpleminded.

19:50.980 --> 19:53.850
You're also a fool as usual.

19:54.760 --> 19:57.320
Our alliance ends here.

19:57.930 --> 20:00.890
You are no longer allowed to
be involved with our work.

20:06.470 --> 20:09.040
All you did was slow me down.

20:09.040 --> 20:12.200
I never saw this as an alliance!

20:12.510 --> 20:13.600
You disappoint me.

20:20.610 --> 20:24.410
Oh, so you know the janitor.

20:24.520 --> 20:25.180
Yes.

20:30.090 --> 20:31.520
Shiro-chan!

20:31.590 --> 20:32.890
You came out again?!

20:33.330 --> 20:34.620
Shiro-chan?

20:34.930 --> 20:36.460
I guess she does look white.

20:36.460 --> 20:39.160
People do say names signify
what things really are, but...

20:39.330 --> 20:41.900
Isn't "Shiro-chan" a bit too predictable?

20:41.900 --> 20:43.490
It almost sounds like you're naming a pet...

20:47.710 --> 20:48.730
Enju-san.

20:49.280 --> 20:52.910
You will have to return her to us, Toru-san.

20:53.080 --> 20:56.610
Why? Why does it have to be Shiro-chan?

20:56.980 --> 20:58.980
Because she signifies the
legitimacy of the lord of the oni.

21:06.290 --> 21:07.760
You need to leave, young lady.

21:14.570 --> 21:15.300
Now!

21:42.260 --> 21:48.720
Sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:49.200 --> 21:56.440
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:57.780 --> 22:04.270
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

22:04.420 --> 22:12.050
Kokoro wa itsumo hane wo hirogetagaru
They always desire to spread
the wings of their hearts.

22:12.960 --> 22:19.990
Yume dakede owarasenai
Don't let it end as just a dream,

22:20.600 --> 22:27.100
chansu ga aru hazusa
There's always a chance.

22:27.310 --> 22:34.750
Daijoubu bokura ha hitori janai
It's all right. We are not alone.

22:34.750 --> 22:42.360
Kaze ga nanika wo iouto shiteru
The winds are telling us something.

22:42.360 --> 22:50.030
Daijoubu kanarazu umaku yareru
It's all right. You can do it.

22:50.030 --> 23:01.270
Omoi wa itsuka jibun wo kaeru michi ni naru
Those dreams are a path you'll change yourself.

23:11.080 --> 23:12.050
This way.

23:12.450 --> 23:14.650
Can we really find him by doing this?

23:15.360 --> 23:17.220
This is no ordinary stick.

23:25.000 --> 23:25.930
Next Time

23:25.930 --> 23:28.970
Next Time
The Byakki assigns anyone
she first sees as her "parent."

23:28.970 --> 23:29.000
Next Time

23:29.000 --> 23:33.570
Next Time
That parent will forever be pursued
by those who desire the Byakki.

23:33.570 --> 23:34.340
Next Time

23:34.340 --> 23:35.180
Next Time
Next time, "Our Fox Deity,
Receives some Memories."

23:35.180 --> 23:36.840
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Receives some Memories
Next time, "Our Fox Deity,
Receives some Memories."

23:36.840 --> 23:37.080
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Receives some Memories

23:37.080 --> 23:39.410
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Receives some Memories
Though we may never meet
again, the memories will remain.

23:39.410 --> 23:39.940
Next Time
Our Fox Deity, Receives some Memories
